From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Will Faust <willtechnoduck@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 13 May 2026 10:30:09 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] iOS ARM64EC: reload REG_CALLRET_SP (x17) before CALL emit
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Native ARM64EC returns clobber x17 (the callret stack pointer). When
FEX falls through to the next CALL emit without first reloading x17
from State.callret_sp, the stp pushing the call-return frame writes
to whatever RX page x17 was left at — a thousand-fault loop in
cross-arch dispatch.

Fix: emit `ldr REG_CALLRET_SP, [STATE, offsetof(callret_sp)]` before
each `stp ..., [x17, -0x10]!` at both CALL emit sites in BranchOps.cpp
(linked-branch path with CallReturnBlock, and SkipFullLookup non-linked
path), guarded #ifdef ARCHITECTURE_arm64ec.

Effect on Thumper iOS port: exception count thousands → 1; reaches
DXMT shader compile, BC texture creation, and FMOD-init code paths
not previously reachable.

Madeira-commit: 48f7eb4130d6f108bf2e7d943d112504f03ceef6
Rebased: clean
Class: madeira-port
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-09-24-fex-latest-rebase.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/JIT/BranchOps.cpp | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/JIT/BranchOps.cpp b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/JIT/BranchOps.cpp
index c2b1d8e..d95e984 100644
--- a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/JIT/BranchOps.cpp
+++ b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/Core/JIT/BranchOps.cpp
@@ -165,6 +165,13 @@ DEF_OP(ExitFunction) {
       ARMEmitter::ForwardLabel l_BranchHost;
       ARMEmitter::ForwardLabel l_CallReturn;
       if (Op->Hint == IR::BranchHint::Call) {
+#ifdef ARCHITECTURE_arm64ec
+        // iOS-Mythic 2026-05-13: REG_CALLRET_SP (x17) gets clobbered when a
+        // previous BLR returns from native ARM64EC code (DXMT vtable methods,
+        // ARM64EC entry thunks). Reload from State.callret_sp before pushing
+        // the call-return frame so we don't stp to wherever x17 was left.
+        ldr(REG_CALLRET_SP, STATE, offsetof(FEXCore::Core::CpuStateFrame, State.callret_sp));
+#endif
         if (!Op->CallReturnBlock.IsInvalid()) {
           auto CallReturnAddressReg = GetReg(Op->CallReturnAddress).X();
           PendingCallReturnTargetLabel = &CallReturnTargets.try_emplace(Op->CallReturnBlock.ID()).first->second;
@@ -220,6 +227,12 @@ DEF_OP(ExitFunction) {
     (void)Bind(&SkipFullLookup);
     if (Op->Hint == IR::BranchHint::Call) {
       ARMEmitter::ForwardLabel l_CallReturn;
+#ifdef ARCHITECTURE_arm64ec
+      // iOS-Mythic 2026-05-13: see note above — reload REG_CALLRET_SP (x17)
+      // from State.callret_sp before pushing the call-return frame, since
+      // native ARM64EC returns leave x17 pointing at an arbitrary RX page.
+      ldr(REG_CALLRET_SP, STATE, offsetof(FEXCore::Core::CpuStateFrame, State.callret_sp));
+#endif
       if (!Op->CallReturnBlock.IsInvalid()) {
         auto CallReturnAddressReg = GetReg(Op->CallReturnAddress).X();
         PendingCallReturnTargetLabel = &CallReturnTargets.try_emplace(Op->CallReturnBlock.ID()).first->second;
